  "method": "Both renderer overlays keep identical size/data. The old branch delay instruction runs first, then a diagnostic BREAK at the end of IMEM. CPU recognizes the BREAK and restores the old branch target, preserving signal bits. For the exchange variant, the second checkpoint of each frame drains the RDP, swaps the selected RSP banks, restores them and verifies all restored words, status and PC. In the task variant a staged two-instruction marker modifies staged DMEM and breaks at its own PC without changing renderer GPR/vector state. The audio DSP remains on the R4300 and keeps processing the original live workload.",
