  "digital_scope": "Frame 88 image (67,200 pixels) and captured audio ring (8,192 bytes) match the same eight-sample live scalar DSP reference in all three runs. Main/Mode 7 overlay layout is proven by the linked checks; the original ordinary-renderer fixture is the physical coverage here. DAC and broad commercial compatibility remain open.",
  "timing_scope": "A running sample after a resume is a lower bound on elapsed time before another checkpoint. The largest observed resume-to-acknowledgment gap includes CPU detection and may be a different interval. Forty in-frame intervals, of which 23 contained running samples. No proof that unsampled intervals fit a bound. A marker task performs no DSP arithmetic and no scalar/vector register save is charged.",
